Merry Christmas this December 25th we  celebrate the birth of Jesus Christ but  was Jesus really born on this day well a  lot of biblical Scholars don't think so  you see in the Gospel of Luke it  describes Shepherds grazing their flocks  this would only have been done in the  spring so by this account Jesus was  probably born in the spring okay so why  do we celebrate in December well poke  Julius the first declared it to be so in  the year 350. why well there are a few  theories the most famous one is that he  set it up to be in line with the Roman  Festival of saturnalia this might be  true but saturnalia was actually held in  mid-December not December 25th a more  likely explanation is that it was placed  to correspond to the winter solstice the  shortest day and longest night of the  year this of course has a lot of  theological symbolism the truth is  though that December 25th is as good a  day as any to celebrate Christmas  because we just don't know and probably  never will know exactly when Jesus was  born so
 

